## Layer 4: Terminal Renderer (carriage-return based)

### Approach: carriage return + ANSI, not a TUI framework

The renderer uses `\r` (carriage return) to overwrite terminal lines
in place. For multi-line display, it uses ANSI cursor-up (`\x1b[A`)
to move back to the top of the display area and rewrite. This gives
a live-updating display without any TUI framework dependency.

The glyph system's Emoji tier is the default — modern emojis make
the display visually striking. We control the environment so
compatibility is not a constraint.

